{
  "description": "Shared contract for the channel editor field that edits the legacy `other` value while a typed config override (config.api_version, config.library_id, config.plugin) may also be stored. The relay prefers a non-empty override over `other` (middleware/distributor.go). Go's encoding/json decodes the override from every top-level config key that equals the override key under strings.EqualFold (underscores stay significant), applying them in document order, so the last string value wins. `stored.spellings` (optional) lists the stored config's override members in document order and may repeat a key; by default the stored config holds `stored.override` under `config_key` (default `override_key`), or no override member when it is null. `stored.override` is always the relay-effective value of the stored config. Every frontend must display `displayed`, and saving with `edit` (null = an unrelated save that leaves the field untouched; a string = the new value typed into the field) must send `payload`: exactly one override member, `config_key` holding `payload.override`, or none when it is null. A stored config that repeats the override key is saved under the canonical `override_key`. The backend must persist `payload` byte for byte, collapse any config that repeats a key into one member holding the relay-effective value, and the relay must then use `effective`. Consumed by Go and frontend tests; do not reformat case names.",
